# Read by alloy.service. Managed from homelab/alloy - edit there, not here.
#
# CONFIG_FILE is the DIRECTORY /etc/alloy, not config.alloy in it: Alloy loads
# every *.alloy file there as one configuration. The fleet file config.alloy
# is byte-identical on all ten hosts; a host that needs more (the loki
# container receives ESXi syslog, see homelab/esxi) drops a second file
# beside it from its own stack, and neither deploy has to know about the
# other. Component names must be unique across the directory.
#
# The package ships CUSTOM_ARGS empty, which makes Alloy listen on
# 127.0.0.1:12345. Prometheus scrapes it from .53, so it has to bind the
# wildcard - and binding the wildcard rather than the host's own IP is also
# what spares it a wait-for-address drop-in. TLS on that listener is in
# config.alloy, not a flag.
CONFIG_FILE="/etc/alloy"
CUSTOM_ARGS="--server.http.listen-addr=0.0.0.0:12345 --disable-reporting"
RESTART_ON_UPGRADE=true
